  "limitations": [
    "Ordinary mode uses unmodified product processor bytes and approximate main-thread/RPC bookends. Its cost is unmeasured, not zero, and its PCM/cost window is not identical to instrumented modes.",
    "Instrumented render means cover original process() including renderInto and stereo copy, not pure WASM or CPU time. Total adds the scan; aggregate updates and boundary state reads remain outside both timers.",
    "All measured clocks were Date.now. The nominal 1ms allowance is an assumption, not a timer precision guarantee. Observed 3ms deltas can straddle the 2.902ms budget; beyond-allowance spans can still include descheduling and do not establish audible or device underruns.",
    "quiet-ui minus timed means were positive in all ten pairs per engine, while capture minus timed render differences had both signs. Two reversed-order repetitions, fresh contexts and uncontrolled OS/power/JIT activity do not isolate causation or prove UI benefit or a capture slowdown.",
    "The old 248/62016 WebKit observation used the research Lab, six subtunes, 30-second captures, a different UI and capture trigger, and lifetime maxima. This study uses the ordinary Player, three original primary tunes plus two synthetic model fixtures, one-second warmup and five-second fixed windows. Rates and maxima are not a direct speedup comparison.",
    "Finite sparse analyser bookends and scalar capture scans do not establish uninterrupted device playback. No human listening, long/background/device/high-load stability or whole-song compatibility is proved."
  ]
